// OLED Dashboard - 4x screens via TCA9548A I2C multiplexer (SD0–SD3)
// Adafruit Feather ESP32-S3 | SDA=GPIO3  SCL=GPIO4 | OLED=0x3C | TCA9548A=0x70
//
// Wiring:
//   Feather STEMMA QT (Qwiic) port
//     → Qwiic cable to TCA9548A breakout
//       → SD0 channel wires → OLED screen 0
//       → SD1 channel wires → OLED screen 1
//       → SD2 channel wires → OLED screen 2
//       → SD3 channel wires → OLED screen 3
//
// Notes:
//   - STEMMA QT on the Feather ESP32-S3 shares Wire (SDA=GPIO3, SCL=GPIO4)
//     with the header pins — no pin change needed.
//   - PIN_I2C_POWER is driven HIGH by enableI2CPower() to power the STEMMA QT rail.
//   - TCA9548A address pins A0/A1/A2 must all be tied LOW for address 0x70.
//   - MAX17048 (battery) and SHT4x (sensor) connect directly on the main I2C
//     bus (not behind the mux), e.g. via a Qwiic T/splitter or header pins.
//
// Screen layout:
//   Channel 0 (SD0): Heart animation GIF
//   Channel 1 (SD1): Clock / time
//   Channel 2 (SD2): Temperature & humidity
//   Channel 3 (SD3): Battery & WiFi status

